CRITICAL: The local development environment uses zsh shell on macOS with Homebrew. Always:

Write scripts with #!/bin/zsh shebang (NOT bash)
Use zsh-compatible syntax and features
Use Homebrew (brew) as the package manager for installing dependencies
Test commands locally before assuming they work
When scripts fail, ALWAYS read and analyze the actual error output
Don't assume scripts work without verification - check the exit codes and output
Use macOS-compatible commands (e.g., brew install instead of apt-get, greadlink instead of readlink)
Be aware of macOS-specific paths and behaviors (e.g., Homebrew installs to /opt/homebrew on Apple Silicon)